Definition:
  CoREHard is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      for every function q from ℕ to Prop satisfying CoRE:
        there is a function r from ℕ to α such that
          r is computable and
          for every natural number n:
            n satisfies q if and only if (r n) satisfies p.

Abbreviation:
  Point is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the type of functions from indices in [0, d) to ℤ.

Abbreviation:
  Prototile is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the type of lists of (Point d) elements.

Definition:
  Adjacent is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element p of Point d and an element q of Point d to
      the sum over indices i in [0, d) of |p i - q i| = 1).

Definition:
  Connected is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      for every x ∈ P:
        for every y ∈ P:
          x is related to y by the reflexive transitive closure of
            (the function mapping an element p of Point d and an element q of Point d to
                p ∈ P and q ∈ P and (p and q satisfy Adjacent)).

Definition:
  Tiles is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      there is a set T of Point d elements such that
        for every element x of Point d:
          there is exactly one t ∈ T such that
            x - t ∈ P.

Theorem tiling_coRE_complete:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
      P satisfies Connected and P satisfies Tiles) satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.CoREComplete
Proof: sorry

Theorem tiling_undecidable:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
      P satisfies Connected and P satisfies Tiles) is not computable
Proof: sorry

Theorem tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        (f T) is a nonempty list and
        (f T) satisfies Connected and
        (T satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) satisfies Tiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4)))
Proof: sorry

Abbreviation:
  RealPoint is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the real Euclidean space of dimension d.

Definition:
  Solid is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      the set of elements x of RealPoint d such that
        there is p ∈ P such that
          for every index i in [0, d):
            p i as a real number ≤ x i and x i ≤ p i as a real number + 1).

Abbreviation:
  Motion is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the type of bijective affine isometries from (RealPoint d) to (RealPoint d) over ℝ.

Definition:
  allMotions is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of all elements of (Motion d).

Definition:
  translations is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        the linear part of f = 1).

Definition:
  translationsAndRotations is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        the determinant of (the linear part of f) = 1).

Definition:
  translationsAndReflections is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        there is t ∈ translations such that
          there is an element p of RealPoint d such that
            there is an element q of RealPoint d such that
              f = t * the reflection across (the perpendicular bisector of p and q).

Definition:
  RealTiles is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d and a set motions of Motion d elements to
      there is a subset T of motions such that
        for almost every element x of RealPoint d:
          there is exactly one f ∈ T such that
            x ∈ the image of (Solid P) under f.

Theorem real_tiling_coRE_hard:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every superset motions of translations:
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P satisfies Connected and (P and motions satisfy RealTiles)) satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.CoREHard
Proof: sorry

Theorem real_tiling_undecidable:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every superset motions of translations:
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P satisfies Connected and (P and motions satisfy RealTiles)) is not computable
Proof: sorry

Theorem real_tiling_coRE_complete:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every motions ∈ the set {allMotions, translations, translationsAndRotations, translationsAndReflections}:
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P satisfies Connected and (P and motions satisfy RealTiles)) satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.CoREComplete
Proof: sorry

Theorem real_tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        (f T) is a nonempty list and
        (f T) satisfies Connected and
        (T satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) satisfies Tiles) and
        ((f T) satisfies Tiles if and only if (f T) and translations satisfy RealTiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4)))
Proof: sorry

Theorem rigid_tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        (f T) is a nonempty list and
        (f T) satisfies Connected and
        (T satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) satisfies Tiles) and
        (for every superset motions of translations:
          (f T) satisfies Tiles if and only if (f T) and motions satisfy RealTiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          2 ^ (10 * (d + 1) ^ 2) *
            (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
              (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4)))
Proof: sorry

Theorem rigid_tiling_reduction_three:
  there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile 3 such that
    f is computable and
    for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
      (f T) is a nonempty list and
      (f T) satisfies Connected and
      (T satisfies LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) satisfies Tiles) and
      (for every superset motions of translations:
        (f T) satisfies Tiles if and only if (f T) and motions satisfy RealTiles) and
      the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
        64000 *
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4)))
Proof: sorry
